{
  "_readme": [
    "Dialogue blip voices, keyed on OVERWORLD SPRITE NAME. See Scripts/Global_Scripts/Speech_Voice.gd.",
    "pitch: 1.0 is the Speech.ogg sample untouched. Lower is deeper (big, heavy, mean, old men);",
    "       higher is lighter (women, and higher again for children).",
    "rate:  blips per letter, relative. 1.0 is normal, 1.3 is a fast chatty kid, 0.7 is a slow elder.",
    "       It does NOT change how fast the text types - that is the player's Text-speed option.",
    "A sprite's numbered alternates and second walk frames (Beauty5, NPCMan_2) fall back to the base",
    "row, so only a genuinely new archetype needs a new entry here. Anything unmatched falls back on",
    "the _F/_M defaults below. Keys are sorted alphabetically; this block is ignored by the loader.",
    "A speaker sprite that is NOT an overworld sprite - a phone call's talking-head costume, or",
    "in-battle art named differently - resolves through the aliases block: a name PREFIX mapped",
    "onto a voices key, longest prefix wins. One alias covers every costume and expression."
  ],
